# Optional HTTPS for the Windows server with Caddy (https://caddyserver.com - one exe, free).
# 1. In C:\InvertedTaskFlow\server.ini set:  bind = 127.0.0.1   and  port = 8080
#    (the unencrypted backend then only answers on this machine - never publish port 8080)
# 2. Put caddy.exe and this file (renamed to Caddyfile) in C:\Caddy, run:  caddy run
#    (install it as a service with:  sc create caddy binPath= "C:\Caddy\caddy.exe run --config C:\Caddy\Caddyfile")
# 3. Desktop apps use https://task.inverted.in:8443 (production name; DNS must point to this server).
#    On first connection they show the certificate fingerprint; compare it with the one Caddy shows in its log,
#    or build the installer with it. "tls internal" keeps one long-lived certificate - do not switch to a
#    public certificate that renews every few months: each renewal changes the pinned fingerprint.
task.inverted.in:8443 {
	tls internal
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080 {
		flush_interval -1
		transport http {
			read_timeout 60s
		}
	}
}
